# APCOTEX Sales Insights — Frontend environment
# Copy to `.env.local` only if you need an explicit API override.
# Never commit secrets. Do not hardcode IPs in source.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# VITE_API_BASE_URL (optional)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# If UNSET: the client auto-derives the API from the browser location:
#   http(s)://<same-hostname>:8000/api
# So localhost, LAN, and VPN/Windows Server IPs all work without code changes.
#
# Set only when the API is on a different host/port than the UI host:8000.
#
# Local override example:
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000/api
#
# Split-host example (UI and API on different machines):
# VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://<API-HOST>:8000/api
#
# Backend CORS_ORIGINS must still include the Origin users open
# (e.g. http://<SERVER-IP>:5173). See backend/.env.example.
